---
import TextPageLayout from '../layouts/TextPageLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const { company, email, legal } = site;
---

<TextPageLayout
  title="Privacy policy — Echo"
  description="How Echo and this website handle personal data. Your recordings and notes stay on your phone; this site sets no cookies."
  updated={legal.updated}
  legal
>
  <section class="summary" aria-labelledby="short">
    <h2 id="short">The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your recordings, transcripts, summaries and tasks are processed and stored only on your phone. We never receive them.</li>
      <li>Echo has no accounts. Payments are handled by Google Play.</li>
      <li>This website sets no cookies and counts visits without identifying you.</li>
      <li>You can contact us any time at <a href={`mailto:${email.privacy}`}>{email.privacy}</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="controller">
    <h2 id="controller">1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      The controller under the GDPR is {company.name}, {company.address}, Slovenia, registration no. {company.regNo},
      VAT ID {company.vatId}. Email: <a href={`mailto:${email.privacy}`}>{email.privacy}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="app">
    <h2 id="app">2. The Echo app</h2>

    <h3>Your recordings and notes</h3>
    <p>
      Audio, transcripts, speaker names, summaries, tasks and folders are created and stored on your device. Speech
      recognition, speaker detection and the Notes AI all run on the phone. Nothing is sent to us or to anyone else
      unless you share or export it yourself. Echo is excluded from Android's cloud backup and device transfer, so your
      notes are not copied to Google either. Backups you make in the app are files you control. Deleting the app, or
      using Delete all data in Settings, removes everything.
    </p>

    <h3>Permissions</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Microphone, to record when you tap Record.</li>
      <li>
        Notifications, exact alarms and starting after a restart, to remind you of tasks at the time you mentioned.
      </li>
      <li>Foreground service, so recording and transcription keep going while the screen is off.</li>
      <li>Internet and network state, only to download models and to buy Pro.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Model downloads</h3>
    <p>
      The speech, speaker and Notes AI models are downloaded when you first set up Echo or choose another model. Your
      phone fetches them from Hugging Face (Hugging Face, Inc., USA) and, for one speaker model, from GitHub (GitHub,
      Inc., USA). Like any download, these servers see your IP address and basic request details, under their own
      privacy policies. Nothing about you or your notes is sent with the request, and we do not receive these logs.
    </p>

    <h3>Purchases</h3>
    <p>
      Pro is sold through Google Play, which processes your payment under <a
        href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a
      >. To know whether you have Pro, the app uses RevenueCat (RevenueCat, Inc., USA) as our processor. RevenueCat
      receives a random, anonymous app user ID, your purchase receipts and history, and basic app and device information
      such as the app version and country of the store. It does not receive your name, email address or payment
      details, and no advertising ID is used. Legal basis: performance of a contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) and legal
      obligations for tax records (Art. 6(1)(c)).
    </p>

    <h3>Crash reports and analytics in the app</h3>
    <p>None. Echo contains no analytics, crash reporting or advertising.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="website">
    <h2 id="website">3. This website</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted by Vercel (Vercel Inc., USA). Their servers process your IP address to deliver the pages and
      keep short-lived logs for security and abuse prevention.
    </p>
    <p>
      We count visits with PostHog, with data stored on PostHog's EU servers in Frankfurt. It runs in cookieless mode:
      it sets no cookies and stores nothing on your device. To tell visits apart for one day, PostHog computes a hash
      from your IP address and browser details with a salt that changes daily, then discards the IP address. We see
      totals such as page views, referring sites and clicks on buttons like Get it on Google Play. Legal basis: our
      legitimate interest in knowing how the site is used (Art. 6(1)(f)).
    </p>
    <p>
      If you press the light/dark switch, your choice is saved in your browser's local storage so the next page opens
      the same way. It never leaves your device and is only there because you asked for it. Because no cookies or
      tracking technologies are used, there is no cookie banner.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="email">
    <h2 id="email">4. When you email us</h2>
    <p>
      If you write to us or use Send feedback in the app, we use your email address and message only to answer you, and
      delete them {legal.emailRetention} after the conversation ends. Our email is handled by {legal.emailProvider}.
      Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) or (f).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="recipients">
    <h2 id="recipients">5. Who else receives data</h2>
    <p>Only the providers named above:</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Role</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Google (Google Play)</td><td>Payments for Pro</td><td>Independent controller</td></tr>
          <tr><td>RevenueCat, Inc.</td><td>Checking Pro purchases</td><td>Processor</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hugging Face, Inc. and GitHub, Inc.</td><td>Model downloads</td><td>Independent controllers</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Vercel Inc.</td><td>Website hosting</td><td>Processor</td></tr>
          <tr><td>PostHog, Inc. (EU hosting)</td><td>Website visit counts</td><td>Processor</td></tr>
          <tr><td>{legal.emailProvider}</td><td>Email</td><td>Processor</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      We have data processing agreements with every processor. Several of these companies are based in the USA. Where
      personal data leaves the EU/EEA, the transfer relies on the EU–US Data Privacy Framework or the European
      Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses. We never sell data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="rights">
    <h2 id="rights">6. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask us for access to, correction, deletion or a copy of your personal data, ask us to restrict its use,
      and object to processing based on legitimate interest. Write to <a href={`mailto:${email.privacy}`}
        >{email.privacy}</a
      >; we answer within one month. Since your notes never reach us, the quickest way to delete them is in the app.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also complain to a supervisory authority. In Slovenia that is the Information Commissioner (Informacijski
      pooblaščenec), Dunajska cesta 22, 1000 Ljubljana, <a href="https://www.ip-rs.si">ip-rs.si</a>, or the authority
      in your own EU country.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="children">
    <h2 id="children">7. Children</h2>
    <p>Echo is intended for people aged {legal.minAge} and over.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="changes">
    <h2 id="changes">8. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, we update the date above. Significant changes are also announced in the app's release
      notes.
    </p>
  </section>
</TextPageLayout>
